# React components

- Use function components and hooks. Type props with an explicit interface. Prefer named exports.
- Compose with `children` and small components. Do not grow boolean prop sets (`isPrimary`, `isCompact`, `hasIcon`) when a new component would be clearer.
- Compute derived values during render. Use `useEffect` to synchronize with an external system, not to copy props into state.
- Extract a custom hook when logic is reused or it obscures the render. Keep the hook in the feature that owns it.
- Use stable domain ids as list keys.
- Add `memo`, `useMemo`, or `useCallback` only after a render cost shows up. Do not memoize by default.
- Do not wrap a single call site in a new component or hook for hypothetical reuse.

```tsx
const priceLabel = formatPrice(listing.price);

useEffect(() => subscribeToListing(listing.id), [listing.id]);
```
